Subject: client: keep the pointer scale when the host restarts

The Looking Glass host in the guest restarts, for example each time the
computer wakes from sleep. On a restart, lgInit set the pointer scale
back to 1.0. Only core_updatePositionInfo sets it again, and the frame
path calls it only for a new frame size or rotation. A new session at
the same size kept the scale at 1.0, so on a display at scale 2 the
window mapped onto the top-left quarter of the guest until the next
resize.

The scale comes from the frame size and the window. A restart by itself
changes neither, and a frame of a new size recomputes the scale. So the
reset now runs only before the client has seen any frame.

- core.c: core_resetPointerScale resets the scale only while haveSrcSize is
  false. The first frame sets haveSrcSize, and nothing clears it.
- main.c: lgInit calls core_resetPointerScale in place of the three writes.
- mouse_test.c: the restart-scale case sets a frame twice the window,
  then checks that a pointer move sends the right position before and
  after the reset, and that a reset before any frame still sets 1.0. It
  stubs the three calls that core_updatePositionInfo needs to link.
- tests/CMakeLists.txt: registers the case.

No message is added and no message's format changes.

